      <p class="feature-row__body">
        Scored by the official <a href="https://github.com/python/typing/blob/main/conformance/results/results.html">python/typing conformance suite</a> &mdash; the same published
        harness that grades Pyright, mypy, and Pyrefly &mdash; run on the real binary with every
        conformance rule enabled and nothing disabled: {{ conformance.categoriesPass100 }} of {{ conformance.categoriesTotal }} categories at 100%,
        {{ conformance.fp }} false positives, {{ conformance.missed }} missed required errors. Every release re-pulls the suite from
        <code>python/typing@main</code> and requires a perfect score to ship, so the number is
        reproducible &mdash; never hand-typed &mdash; and always graded against the exact commit shown below.
        Basilisk is now <a href="{{ conformanceOfficial.snapshot.source }}">listed in the official python/typing results</a> &mdash; graded on the same run as every other checker, it is the only one at a perfect {{ conformanceOfficial.basilisk.pct }}%, ahead of the tools from Microsoft, Meta and Astral.
      </p>
