        mypy, ty, Pyrefly, and zuban on identical fixtures &mdash; and the raw CSV is committed to
        the repo, so the site renders exactly what was last measured.
        {% if benchmarks.toolMedians.fastest == 'basilisk' %}Basilisk posts the fastest cold full-file check of every tool we measured &mdash; a
        {{ benchmarks.toolMedians.ms.basilisk }}&nbsp;ms median, up to {{ benchmarks.vsPyright.maxFactor }}&times; faster than Pyright.{% else %}On the constructs we benchmark, Basilisk&rsquo;s cold full-file checks beat Pyright outright.{% endif %}
        And because re-checks are incremental &mdash; only the edited file and its importers are
